       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. It is also well above the 2,000 mg maximum for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also higher than the usual labeled maximum single dose of 1,000 mg (immediate-release).\n\nThe dose may be a typo. 1700 mg per day, or 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), would be within the labeled limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day split into doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen.** Tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nTell me which you want and I'll enter it right away."
