       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, I'm not able to enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose. 5,100 mg/day is twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n\nThe usual route for a dose like this is to have the prescriber enter it directly. That lets pharmacy review it and the prescriber document the override. Metformin also carries a lactic acidosis risk, and doses above the labeled maximum have no added glucose-lowering benefit.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum).\n- **Another dose within labeled limits.**\n\nIf the specialist wants a different approach, such as adding or switching to another agent, the prescriber can specify it and I can enter that order."
      }
